Package: lifeline
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Vikram Aggarwal <vikram@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), dnsmasq-base, nftables, iproute2, network-manager
Recommends: systemd-resolved
Suggests: python3-gi, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicatorglib-2.0, libnotify-bin
Description: Wi-Fi-aware Ethernet DHCP router and automatic failover daemon
 Lifeline turns a Linux laptop with Wi-Fi and Ethernet into a fail-safe,
 self-coordinating gateway on a shared Ethernet cable or switch:
  * PRIMARY mode: when Wi-Fi is healthy and no other DHCP server owns the
    wire, configures Ethernet with a static IP, starts dnsmasq using a
    hardware-MAC-to-IP table, and enables IPv4/IPv6 NAT + forwarding only
    for active DHCP clients.
  * SECONDARY mode: when Wi-Fi is healthy and another DHCP server (external
    router or another lifeline laptop) is active, stays in standby and
    promotes via deterministic election if the primary disappears.
  * FAILOVER mode: when Wi-Fi fails, stops DHCP serving, blocks Ethernet
    forwarding, configures Ethernet via DHCP client (gateway + DNS), and
    probes Wi-Fi via a dedicated policy routing table until recovery.
